[ext_resource type="Texture2D" path="res://assets/bonelight/ui/spells/hollow-star-dark.png" id="3_icon"]

; The pull spell (issue #64). A well opens in the thickest pack within BaseRange, drags everything
; within its reach into one knot, then collapses on what it gathered. Pure Darkness: the element had
; no pure spell, so it could never reach its capstone.
;
; Effect 7 (AreaSize) widens the pull reach in pixels; Effect 13 (ZoneDuration) lengthens the pull
; in seconds. Both are read in Player.FireHollowStar.
;
; 0.9.3 (Eric's playtest of 0.9.2: "reduce the cooldown on hollow star, it's very powerful" - read as
; fire LESS often): cooldown 4.5 -> 6.0 s (5.1 at level 8, was 3.6). The damage line 18 / +5 / +6 / +8
; -> 8 / +2 / +3 / +8 (10 at level 4, 13 at 6, 21 at 8): what the collapse deals at its core, falling
; to about a third at its edge (HollowStar.ShareAt), so a knotted enemy takes 10 at level 4 where it
; took 23. In the 8-minute bot the spell kills all it catches, so its damage a second follows
; the hit, not the cooldown - the longer cooldown only lets more gather. .ai/spell-roster.md section 2e.

